{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nNo document tells a client project how to run plan-replay, fixture-mining or provider-parity against its own `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` and `.rebar/evals/`. `docs/llm-framework.md`'s \"Extras taxonomy\" (`:43`) still opens \"The optional surface is three extras\" (`:45`) — a count that was already stale and is now wrong by two: sibling story `d279` (`disgusted-fretful-hare`, closed) registered `evals` in `rebar._optional.EXTRAS`.\n\nSeparately, 71 open, parentless `fixture-drift:` tasks (e.g. `00b4-b253-3052-4181`) were filed by hand for story 67aa from `evals/plan-review-gate/fixtures/drift-report.md`, each `discovered_from` the closed epic `65dd-e93b-666a-4caa`. `git grep fixture-drift` is empty; `fixture_mining/heal.py`'s only ticket producer is `_file_unreliable_ticket` (`UNRELIABLE_TITLE_PREFIX` at `heal.py:32`, consumed at `:273`), and drift is written to `.rebar/fixture_heal_drift.md` (`heal.py:426`). Those 71 tasks have no producer and no consumer. Cites verified on `aa37a738570` plus the corpus move.\n\n**Scope correction — the extras REGISTRATION is already done.** `d279` added the `evals` key to `EXTRAS`, routed `genai_prices` through `guard_import`, and added the `evals:evals` spec to `.github/workflows/_optionality.yml`. This story's remaining work on that axis is DOCUMENTING the extra, not registering it; the title's \"register the evals extra\" is satisfied upstream and no AC here re-asserts it.\n\n## Approach\nAdd a `docs/llm-framework.md` section \"Running the eval harnesses against your own criteria\" after \"Usage log\" (`:471`), covering: install with `pip install 'nava-rebar[agents,evals]'`; criteria in `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` and project prompts in `.rebar/prompts/<id>.md` (override-wins ordering, `fixture_selection.rubric_path` `:38`, override branch `:52-54`); specs in `.rebar/evals/<prompt_id>.eval.yaml` beating packaged ones (`eval.py:57-78`); `[llm.evals] corpus_root` (default `.rebar/evals`, env `REBAR_LLM_EVALS_CORPUS_ROOT`).\n\nThen the commands: `rebar prompt eval <prompt_id>`; `rebar criteria eval [<criterion_id>] --changed-since origin/main --require-live`; `rebar criteria heal --dry-run` then `rebar criteria heal` (`cap_usd=25.0`, passed to `production_attempter` at `_llm_eval_commands.py:136`; writes `.rebar/fixture_heal_drift.md`, `.rebar/fixture_heal_ledger.jsonl`, emits `.rebar/evals/*.eval.yaml`, files `unreliable-criterion: <id>` tickets); `python -m rebar.llm.evals.plan_replay tier0 --candidate current`, `tier1 --n 20`, `tier2 --criteria E1` (writing under `<corpus_root>/plan-review-gate/replay/`, `--store name=path` for another store, `--ledger` to relocate spend); `python -m rebar.llm.evals.provider_parity --slot standard --epochs 3 --out <path>`.\n\n**`--out` has no default and is not corpus-root-relative.** `provider_parity.py:604` declares `default=None` and the write at `:649-651` is guarded by `if args.out:`, so a run without it writes nothing. `d279` deliberately left that flag unchanged, so the doc must show `--out` explicitly rather than implying an automatic location — and the release note must not claim otherwise.\n\nUpdate the taxonomy's opening count at `:45` and add an `evals` bullet; add the `llm.evals.corpus_root` row to \"Configuration\" (`:395`); add a `[llm.evals]` snippet to `docs/llm-example-configs.md`.\n\n**Disposition of the 71 tasks**, through the MCP server: for each id from `search(\"title:fixture-drift: status:open\")`, `transition_ticket(id, \"open\", \"closed\", close_class=\"obsolete\", reason=\"superseded by the scheduled fixture-heal loop (rebar criteria heal, heal.py), which re-mines every criterion on fixture_heal.interval_days, records drift in .rebar/fixture_heal_drift.md, and files one unreliable-criterion: ticket per criterion failing three consecutive re-mines; per-entry drift tickets have no producer and no consumer\")`. `obsolete` is reason-required administrative vocabulary minting a disposition verdict with no LLM run. Then `comment_ticket(\"65dd-e93b-666a-4caa\", ...)` recording the batch.\n\nRelease note (non-breaking, contract section): eval harness roots are configurable (`llm.evals.corpus_root`, default `.rebar/evals`); `plan_replay.ledger.DEFAULT_LEDGER_PATH` removed, ledger defaults resolving at call time; the `evals` extra is registered. No claim about `--out`.\n\n**The doc test is generated from one source, not a hand-kept list.** Sibling story `bafa` needed six plan-review rounds because hand-enumerated references kept drifting. So `tests/unit/test_llm_framework_docs.py` derives its expectations from the data: the extras assertion iterates `rebar._optional.EXTRAS` (so a future extra fails the doc, not the test), and the command assertions read the fenced command block out of the section and compare against a module-level tuple that the test itself also uses to shell out with `--help`, so a renamed flag fails rather than silently passing.\n\n## Scope\n`docs/llm-framework.md`, `docs/llm-example-configs.md`, `docs/release-notes.md`, `tests/unit/test_llm_framework_docs.py` (new); tracker writes on the 71 tickets plus one comment. No source files, and nothing under `evals/`.\n\n## Testing\n`pytest tests/unit/test_llm_framework_docs.py -q`; `python scripts/check_docs_index.py`; each documented command run once in a temp client repo (`rebar init`, copy `.rebar/criteria_routing.json`), using `--dry-run` where offered. Edge: `rebar prompt eval nonexistent-id` names the missing spec path rather than raising a traceback; re-running the disposition batch is a no-op, each ticket already closed, so exit 10 is expected and skipped.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `docs/llm-framework.md` contains the section heading, and every command in its fenced block resolves — each one's `--help` exits 0, asserted by `test_llm_framework_docs.py`.\n- [ ] Every key in `rebar._optional.EXTRAS` appears in the extras taxonomy, asserted by iterating `EXTRAS` rather than against a literal count, and the taxonomy's opening sentence no longer says \"three extras\".\n- [ ] `llm.evals.corpus_root` is documented with its default `.rebar/evals` and its env name `REBAR_LLM_EVALS_CORPUS_ROOT`.\n- [ ] The documented `provider_parity` invocation passes `--out` explicitly, and neither the doc nor the release note claims a default output location.\n- [ ] `rebar search \"fixture-drift:\" -o json | jq '[.[]|select(.status==\"open\")]|length'` prints `0`, and each closed record carries `close_class: obsolete` with the reason.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.\n"}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793106684334236001,"uuid":"1237c24b-e019-408f-8eef-b0d854972567"}